hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer a question from one of  my Facebook viewers Jasmine who wrote in  a really really long message it's almost  a page here a message I won't read the  whole thing but the crux of it is I know  in my heart in mind that it takes money  to make money how do you make money if  you don't have the finance system to  back it up and that's the key thing I  wanted to address today I want to get  that notion out of your head it doesn't  take money to make money it's not about  how many resources you have it's about  how resourceful you can be so if you  look at all the the famous successful  entrepreneurs especially in the past a  lot of them didn't come from wealthy  backgrounds all of them didn't have huge  investors the bootstrap their way up you  know they make the tough decisions and  did not go out and spend a lot of money  and the key here is not spending until  you're making money anybody can spend  money right if I give you a hundred  thousand dollars you can go out and  spend it but how can you go out and make  that hundred thousand dollars for your  business that's the key and you don't  want to start spending a lot of money  until you know you can make some money  back so forever business you're starting  try to figure out a way to get it  started with just your time get close to  your customers talk to them about  potential problems they're having and  try to start with a service because the  service doesn't cost you anything except  your time to get gone you don't need  expensive business cards you don't need  an office you don't need a website even  to get started you can just get started  and if you see that you're getting  progress on it then you can start  investing a little bit of the money that  comes in even if it's a little bit you  invest a tiny bit of money back into the  project that you're starting with i put  the example like uses these videos so  when i first started i wanted to do it  because I was passionate about it or  they decided I liked helping  entrepreneurs people are asking  questions and I want to be able to  respond in a way that could help them  but also help other people who are  facing the same problem but I didn't  want to go out and spend a lot of money  on equipment and you know  camera and everything to get everything  started it's not that I couldn't do it I  just didn't want to because for any new  project that we're doing we always have  to find a way to make it profitable  before we start investing a lot of money  into it and it could have bought the  best camera the best gear done two  videos hated it and then you know I have  wasted all this money on it and that  that happens in a lot of startups you  have an idea one week in another idea  another week another idea another week  and you can spend so much money by an  inventory buying equipment and products  whatever it is and nothing ever ends up  taking off so when you're doing that  discovery process you want to invest  your time to make sure there's an  opportunity but not spend a lot of money  doing it so for me you can go back to my  youtube channel you can look at a whole  bunch of really bad videos you know that  the quality of the content was pretty  good but the lighting was bad the camera  was bad the sound was bad I didn't have  a microphone and then as I figured out a  way to get them sponsored and get some  monetization then I could invest more  into the video so it can get a better  camera and get lighting and get us  stained and get you know microphone and  all the things that you need to be able  to make the quality a little bit better  but those old videos they still get some  good views anyways so I'm as much as I  may look back at them and shudder at how  bad they look there was still some good  value and people enjoy them so for you  you got to just get started with the  service start something really small get  close to your customers try to figure  out a way you can help them build  something around what you're really  passionate about you feel you can add a  lot of value to people's lives and help  them solve an important problem in their  lives and then from there you know  investing money back into your business  continue to grow and bootstrap your way  up if you find that you're able to make  a little bit of money off of you know so  just a time that you have then there may  be an opportunity to go for investment  to rapidly grow that's part of your plan  but you don't need to like I'd really  start the focus for any new entrepreneur  is get to the survival point right you  got to get to the point where you're  able to pay your bills put food on the  table you may not be rich right you know  you're not rolling in it yet you know  how to buying out you know the new car  the new house yet but you got to get to  the point where you don't have to go get  a job right you're you're enjoying what  you're doing and you're able to earn  enough money to pay for your you know  living expenses that's step one that's  what you got to get to before you risk  going out and trying to grow too quickly  and invest a whole lot of money into it  once you get past the vagal point if you  see them a way to grow you can keep  doing what you're doing there may be  ways to ramp it up and get some  investment and continue to grow but I  first try to get to that survival point  and try not to spend any money till  you're making money and do it through  providing a service remember the the  value that you provide is going to  determine how much money you make if you  want to make a lot of money you got to  provide a lot of value to your customers  and the reward you so hopefully that  helps and answers your question if you  guys watching like the video please give  it a thumbs up below it makes me want to  do more of these for you and if you have  a question about you know making money  your resources or anything else about  your business feel free to leave it in  comments below I always read them and I  almost always reply so thank you and  you'll see you on the next episode  you  you
 

